{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04I8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f_c^{-1}$", "MATH_0002": "$$\nf^{-1}\\mathcal{H} \\times_{h_{u(V)}^\\#, c} h_U^\\# \\times_{h_U^\\#} h_{U'}^\\#\n=\nf^{-1}(\\mathcal{H} \\times_{h_V^\\#} h_{V'}^\\#)\n\\times_{h_{u(V'), c'}^\\#} h_{U'}^\\#\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$f^{-1}h_V^\\# = h_{u(V)}^\\#$", "MATH_0004": "$f^{-1}h_{V'}^\\# = h_{u(V')}^\\#$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-relocalize}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-localize-morphism}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-relocalize-explicit}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-localize-morphism}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-pullback-representable-sheaf}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fcdb42b2acad6f55405b4c529a9a521f87a2b89c7260863850ab72359b67a907", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5090f60fdb63468dd7b43a9a950774684655f1b6afe64000887e852e6d3590c5", "source_text": "This lemma proves itself, and is more a collection of things we know\nat this stage of the development of theory. For example the commutativity\nof the first square follows from the commutativity of\nDiagram (<REF_0001>)\nand the commutativity of the diagram in\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nThe description of <MATH_0001> follows on combining\nLemma <REF_0003>\nwith\nLemma <REF_0004>.\nThe commutativity of the last square then follows from the\nequality\n<MATH_0002>\nwhich is formal using that <MATH_0003> and\n<MATH_0004>, see\nLemma <REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cf70bf2671ed98f0307594745d66405ac8c90ef94c4d38b7d64d29cdadd92f81", "unit_id": "tag:04IN:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04I8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f'_*j_U^{-1} = j_V^{-1}f_*$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-localize-morphism}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-localize-morphism}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dd4de59a4d5fdaffceeff9355615ef5acd92f5bbaf479e45df5a1f2717d093b1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8a548f47c765216793c2b1f6996bcd7d09377a330e462cceb43dbd583d4ed0eb", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the following lemma we find another kind of functoriality of\nlocalization, in case the morphism of topoi comes from a\ncocontinuous functor. This is a kind of diagram which is different\nfrom the diagram in\nLemma <REF_0001>,\nand in particular, in general the equality <MATH_0001> seen in\nLemma <REF_0002>\ndoes not hold in the situation of the following lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e3517b6988d1d07fc7d99ecc55235f297e236fc36e6855e92e05cf8394ff0457", "unit_id": "tag:04I8:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04I8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0003": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$V = u(U)$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{C}/U \\ar[r]_{j_U} \\ar[d]_{u'} & \\mathcal{C} \\ar[d]^u \\\\\n\\mathcal{D}/V \\ar[r]^-{j_V} & \\mathcal{D}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$u' : \\mathcal{C}/U \\to \\mathcal{D}/V$", "MATH_0009": "$U'/U \\mapsto V'/V$", "MATH_0010": "$u'$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}/U) \\ar[r]_{j_U} \\ar[d]_{f'} &\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}) \\ar[d]^f \\\\\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}/V) \\ar[r]^-{j_V} &\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{D})\n}\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$f$", "MATH_0013": "$f'$", "MATH_0014": "$u$", "MATH_0015": "$u'$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-localize-cocontinuous}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ffecf2a11e3ddc2253742d45176e1d50f76cdc3cc24c186fc9b1c2c9e876b68f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:59b3955b0503ca2f9a9f921ab9bec198484abdb1dc3d27d5f32813969479e271", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> be sites.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a cocontinuous functor.\nLet <MATH_0004> be an object of <MATH_0005>, and set <MATH_0006>.\nWe have a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0007>\nwhere the left vertical arrow is\n<MATH_0008>, <MATH_0009>.\nThen <MATH_0010> is cocontinuous also and we get a commutative diagram of topoi\n<MATH_0011>\nwhere <MATH_0012> (resp.<SPACE_0001><MATH_0013>) corresponds to <MATH_0014> (resp.<SPACE_0002><MATH_0015>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aa7822564606974fab14ff743f883fd0aefab392f0ddb3d9d6f7654c2c960cff", "unit_id": "tag:03EG:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04I8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u'$", "MATH_0002": "$U'/U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{V_j/V \\to u(U')/V\\}_{j \\in J}$", "MATH_0005": "$u(U')/V$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{D}/V$", "MATH_0007": "$u$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{U_i' \\to U'\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{u(U_i') \\to u(U')\\}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\{V_j \\to u(U')\\}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\alpha : I \\to J$", "MATH_0013": "$\\phi_i : u(U_i') \\to V_{\\alpha(i)}$", "MATH_0014": "$U'$", "MATH_0015": "$U_i'$", "MATH_0016": "$U$", "MATH_0017": "$U'_i \\to U' \\to U$", "MATH_0018": "$\\{U'_i/U \\to U'/U\\}$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0020": "$\\{u(U_i')/V \\to u(U')/V\\}$", "MATH_0021": "$\\{V_j/V \\to u(U')/V\\}$", "MATH_0022": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0023": "$\\phi_i$", "MATH_0024": "$u' : \\mathcal{C}/U \\to \\mathcal{D}/V$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:20fd81e1240389f4a32c59f48fda6c49ec49b2a443f76211925e49f6501c2494", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5db83f3c78835e34e5e6645043f2e8a5b40cf07bad0e0eaab22edae0e515c94b", "source_text": "The commutativity of the first diagram is clear.\nIt implies the commutativity of the second diagram provided we\nshow that <MATH_0001> is cocontinuous.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nLet <MATH_0002> be an object of <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a covering of <MATH_0005>\nin <MATH_0006>. Since <MATH_0007> is cocontinuous there exists a\ncovering <MATH_0008> such that the family\n<MATH_0009> refines the covering\n<MATH_0010> in <MATH_0011>. In other words, there exists\na map of index sets <MATH_0012> and morphisms\n<MATH_0013> over <MATH_0014>.\nThink of <MATH_0015> as an object over\n<MATH_0016> via the composition <MATH_0017>. Then\n<MATH_0018> is a covering of <MATH_0019> such that\n<MATH_0020> refines <MATH_0021>\n(use the same <MATH_0022> and the same maps <MATH_0023>). Hence\n<MATH_0024> is cocontinuous.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4f0083072b49eebc873d9904acbf892fbfa971e19c0eaf839d6c91e0a96b046e", "unit_id": "tag:03EG:proof"}
